# Alpha OS — PPAs — Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (resolute)
#
# This file intentionally contains ZERO package names.
#
# A PPA is not a package: it is an apt source (a signed extra `deb` line) plus
# a signing key. It therefore cannot be expressed as a package-list line, and
# putting an `add-apt-repository ppa:...` line here would be invalid syntax for
# live-build's package list parser (which accepts bare package names only, one
# per line, with `#` comments).
#
# Instead, every PPA is added by `config/hooks/50-ppas.chroot`, which is
# run fail-softly: a dead or missing PPA logs a warning and is skipped. It must
# never fail the ISO build.
#
# The PPA set considered for Alpha OS — ALL UNVERIFIED for resolute, since
# PPAs are not part of the released suite and none of these was confirmed to
# carry a `resolute` (or `questing`/`plucky` successor) series:
#   ppa:kubuntu-ppa/backports
#   ppa:kubuntu-ppa/ppa
#   ppa:ubuntu-desktop/ppa
#   ppa:cinnamon-team/ppa
#   ppa:xfce-gooders/ppa
#   ppa:pipewire-debian/pipewire-upstream   <- this is a DEBIAN PPA; it may
#                                               have no resolute suite at all
# Because none is verified, none of them may be a hard dependency of the build.
#
# Constraints honoured by the hook:
#   * fail-soft: unreachable PPA => warning, build continues;
#   * nothing installed from a PPA may break `--debian-installer live`
#     (the installer path must remain installable from the official suite);
#   * package installs in this file are restricted to names that also exist in
#     the official resolute suite, so a missing PPA can never remove packages.
